Found by the k61 audit. (1) examples/service/usage_schema.sql lacks requested_model, cached_tokens, cache_write_tokens, content_bytes, cost_cache_* that share/sql/usage_events.postgresql.sql has; prepare() heals it with auto_migrate, but the example is stale -- sync it with share/sql or drop it in favour of share/sql. (2) init-skeid.sh writes customer keys to secret/skeid/customer/<name> in OpenBao, but no Skeid code reads them (customer key id = digest of the presented key, ADR 0008/0011/0016); the example implies an auth that does not exist. Make the example show what Skeid actually does (names: section / keyid).

More from the k60 README audit (compose stack): skeid service uses image tag :test while init uses :latest; SKEID_USAGE_DB is set to a PostgreSQL DSN but is a SQLite path variable; SKEID_REMOTE_KEY_REF is read by nothing; init never writes the groq key the sample node refers to; init job and healthcheck use psql and curl which the image may not install (init would wait for psql forever); BAO_DEV_ROOT_TOKEN probably should be BAO_DEV_ROOT_TOKEN_ID (unverified). Also examples/vast-start.sh prints http://0.0.0.0:0.0.0.0:8090/v1. README.md 'Service stack' section documents these caveats -- update it when fixing.

